  <h1 class="mb-5 mt-0 font-serif text-4xl font-semibold leading-tight text-base-content sm:text-[2.8rem]">State Availability</h1>

  <div class="answer-first">
    <span class="af-label">In short</span>
    <p><strong>About 36 states plus DC are treated as open to sweepstakes casinos; 14 are closed.</strong> Eleven are closed by statute (California, New York, Connecticut, Indiana, Louisiana, Maine, Montana, Nevada, New Jersey, Oklahoma and Tennessee) and three by enforcement (Idaho, Michigan and Washington). California closed most recently, on 1 January 2026 under AB 831.</p>
    <p>All research on this site is public everywhere. Commercial offers appear only after you select a state, and are blocked for states where sweepstakes casinos are closed by statute or enforcement.</p>
  </div>

  <h2>How the gate works on this site</h2>
  <p>Select your state below. Your choice is stored on your device for 30 days and controls only whether affiliate links are displayed; it never changes which articles you can read.</p>

  <section class="eligibility" aria-label="State selection">
    <h2>Your state</h2>
    <p>Stored locally for 30 days. Nothing is sent to us.</p>
    <div class="js-only">
